    {
      "title": "Function.Semiconj",
      "name": "Function.Semiconj",
      "kind": "def",
      "module": "Mathlib.Logic.Function.Conjugate",
      "line": 29,
      "statement": "def Semiconj (f : α → β) (ga : α → α) (gb : β → β) : Prop",
      "doc_comment": "We say that `f : α → β` semiconjugates `ga : α → α` to `gb : β → β` if `f ∘ ga = gb ∘ f`.\nWe use `∀ x, f (ga x) = gb (f x)` as the definition, so given `h : Function.Semiconj f ga gb` and\n`a : α`, we have `h a : f (ga a) = gb (f a)` and `h.comp_eq : f ∘ ga = gb ∘ f`.",
      "source_sha256": "e5e3aa3e4f3fcbcf97d7c7b33e1be84a1333608f483d30cdcc423a09dfe7bc98",
      "extraction": "textual_unverified",
      "proof_status": "not_checked",
